From: Crystal Forge maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] libstore: opt in to authority-bound netrc reads (Nix 2.35)

Netrc matches hostname, not scheme or port, and libcurl can reload netrc
credentials after a redirect. Confine CF Basic read subprocesses before curl
can perform any transfer. Leave ordinary Nix transfers unchanged.

Classify CF policy refusals as Misc, not Forbidden: the HTTP binary-cache
reader converts Forbidden into missing-file results. Misc preserves the
static policy error. Preflight refusals never enqueue a transfer; HTTP 3xx
refusals call fail directly without entering transient retry handling.

